WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:04.870
Days out from the release of the comic book
antihero movie Venom, several news outlets

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.820
have obtained some juicy bits of info about
the movie's two post-credits scenes, as well

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.620
as one big reveal that would tie into a potential
sequel.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:16.760
So what does the Tom Hardy-starring, Ruben
Fleischer -directed movie have in store for

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:17.260
viewers?

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.240
Grab a snack and check it out.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:22.400
"So many snacks, so little time."

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:28.540
Now, for those of you who want to walk into
Venom knowing just the basics about what will

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.100
go down, we advise you avert your eyes.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:35.040
If these reports of the post-credits scenes
turn out to be the real deal, then they're

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:39.720
set up to spoil not just what will happen,
but also what definitely won't happen during

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.220
the movie.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.480
One more time, for anyone not paying attention:
major spoilers ahead.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.180
According to a report from MCU Cosmic, the
first Venom post-credits scene will see Hardy's

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:54.889
Eddie Brock miraculously maintaining his job
as a journalist, even after transforming into

00:00:54.889 --> 00:00:56.840
the people-eating, fang-toothed Venom.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.659
Eddie, hungry to chase down new leads and
cover a fresh story after his wild investigation

00:01:01.659 --> 00:01:05.820
of the Life Foundation, reportedly travels
to San Quentin prison to interview a very

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:11.450
special inmate: Cletus Kasady, the serial
killer better known in Marvel Comics as Carnage.

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:15.660
Kasady, as has long been rumored, will in
fact be played by Woody Harrelson, with his

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:18.220
involvement in the movie having been intended
as a secret.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:24.520
Harrelson will reportedly sport a comics-accurate
red-headed look by donning a ginger wig, lurking

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.720
in police custody as a looming menace.

00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:31.880
When approached by Eddie Brock, Cletus asks
if he, quote, "wants to hear the carnage"

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:33.040
of the murders he's committed.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.220
You heard right:

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.780
"Carnage!"

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:40.900
That's a grade-A, by-the-comic-books tease
for a sequel if we've ever seen one.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:45.300
So if Venom does even halfway decently at
the box office, it looks like a follow-up

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.600
should be coming in hot.

00:01:46.990 --> 00:01:51.480
The possibility of Harrelson's involvement
as Carnage has been circulating for months.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.920
After plenty of speculation and uncertainty,
Harrelson finally broke his silence by confirming

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.040
his involvement in the movie as well as an
untitled sequel.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.100
Speaking to Collider in May 2018, Harrelson
said,

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:05.600
"I'm in a little fraction of this movie, but
I'll be in the next one, you know?"

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:10.660
Prior to Harrelson's remarks, there was speculation
that Carnage a well-known adversary of both

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.480
Venom and Spider-Man would be the main villain
of the movie.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:18.610
But That Hashtag Show published reports claiming
that Kasady would mostly appear in the post-credits

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.780
tease claims which these new reports seem
to confirm.

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:26.900
The outlet cited an unnamed source saying
that Kasady would be in the custody of Ravencroft

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:31.380
Institute founder Dr. Ashley Kafka, a Marvel
Comics character who is highly experienced

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.700
in treating criminally insane super-people.

00:02:33.980 --> 00:02:38.560
That source also relayed that during Eddie's
talk with Kasady, a part of the Venom symbiote

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:41.680
starts lurching toward him before the screen
cuts to black.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:46.440
This suggests that somewhere between the first
and second Venom movies, Kasady will obtain

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.860
a symbiote of his own, thus becoming the villain
known as Carnage.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:54.400
If true, this would align with the Marvel
Comics lore, in which Kasady transforms into

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.680
the beastly entity after a prison breakout.

00:02:57.430 --> 00:03:02.980
As for the second post-credits scene, it reportedly
opens with a scrawl of text, reading, "Meanwhile,

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:04.260
in another Spider-Verse…"

00:03:04.570 --> 00:03:08.740
It then launches into a sneak peek at Sony's
upcoming animated feature, Spider-Man: Into

00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:14.099
the Spider-Verse, which centers on Miles Morales,
Gwen Stacy, an older Peter Parker, and more

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.800
alternate universe Spider-People.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:20.120
This scene should be arguably less exciting
than the first one, since it isn't directly

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.220
related to Venom, but it should nonetheless
put a smile on the faces of Spider-fans.

00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:27.120
Still, it's hard not to be a little disappointed.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:31.599
Post-credits scenes are all basically just
ads for upcoming movies, but this sounds like

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:35.550
it's literally just an advertisement for another
Sony flick, and we can't imagine that will

00:03:35.550 --> 00:03:38.520
thrill too many people after sitting through
ten minutes of credits.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:39.260
But hey!

00:03:39.640 --> 00:03:41.380
At least the movie looks pretty great.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:46.260
So, now that we probably know what the Venom
post-credits scenes will entail, when during

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:48.220
those credits can viewers expect to see them?

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.260
According to MCU Cosmic, the first scene is
a more traditional, mid-credits scene that

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:55.890
will start not too long after the movie itself
ends.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:04:00.470
The second the Spider-Verse tease is reportedly
at the very end of the credits, serving as

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:02.620
a little bonus for the people who've stuck
around.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.880
Screen Rant - however - is reporting it a
little differently - the additional bits of

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:09.140
footage will actually play out back-to-back.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.410
Until the movie comes out, it's hard to say
for certain, but it sounds like these two

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.700
scenes are the only scenes to watch out for.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:20.019
Of course, at this point, almost two decades
into superhero mania, many audiences are conditioned

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:22.480
not to go anywhere until the staff is sweeping
the theater.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:27.740
Last-minute surprises are still possible,
so that's the only way to be 100% sure you

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:28.340
saw everything.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.780
But as of now, it's almost certain: Carnage
is coming.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:33.080
...Eventually.

